  "seoBody": "<p>Your firm can have multiple people on the dashboard. Each person is either an <strong>admin</strong> or a <strong>member</strong>.</p><h2>Roles</h2><p>Both admins and members can view engineers, workflows and submissions. The following actions are restricted to admins only and are not available to members:</p><ul><li>Add or remove engineers</li><li>Create or edit workflows</li><li>Send workflows to engineers</li><li>Manage billing and plan</li><li>Invite or remove team members</li><li>Change another person's role</li></ul><h2>Inviting someone</h2><ol><li>Go to the <strong>Team</strong> section of the dashboard.</li><li>Enter their email address and click <strong>Invite</strong>.</li><li>They receive an email with a link. The link expires after 7 days.</li></ol><p>New team members join as admins by default. Change their role after they accept.</p><h2>Changing roles</h2><p>Click the role toggle next to a team member's name. You cannot demote yourself if you are the only admin.</p><h2>Removing someone</h2><p>Click <strong>Remove</strong> next to their name. They lose access immediately. Their historical actions (workflow sends, submissions) are preserved.</p><p>Still stuck? Email <a href=\"mailto:hello@quickler.co\">hello@quickler.co</a> and we reply within one business day.</p>",
